@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s348e-civic-expiry`

-- TESTS for priority 1 of row IL-34: the National-Civic Service Law's expiry (s 36) and the temporary text
-- of National Insurance Law s 348(e). Every expected value below was worked out by hand from the two texts
-- BEFORE this module was run. The printed day is 31.8.2026 (civic line 330); written D below.
--
-- Hand rules used:
--   in force on a day d, if the Law stands until E:  d before E yes; d after E no; d = E: by the day-reading.
--   s 36(b): the Law applies to one serving on d who began before E (strictly), or if it is in force on d.
--   s 348(e) temporary text reaches a person who began on s for a span: the span's last day is on or
--     before E (yes); s before E (yes); the span's first day is after E (no); otherwise the span straddles E
--     (declined). The span's last day is the day before the first of the month after its last month.
--   At the switch (every reading declined) a question is answered only where the printed-day answer is
--   TRUE (it never falls as the day moves later), or where the readings it stands for agree.

§ `Tests: the Civic Service Law's expiry`

§§ `Fixtures`

`the deposited expiry, the day itself in force` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `the expiry stays as the deposited text states it`
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the Law is in force through the expiry day`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `the temporary text ends with the Civic Service Law, whenever that is`

`the deposited expiry, the day itself out of force` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `the expiry stays as the deposited text states it`
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the Law ends at the start of the expiry day`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `the temporary text ends with the Civic Service Law, whenever that is`

`moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text following` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `a later Act moved the expiry to` (YMD 2027 8 31)
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the Law is in force through the expiry day`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `the temporary text ends with the Civic Service Law, whenever that is`

`moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text fixed` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `a later Act moved the expiry to` (YMD 2027 8 31)
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the Law is in force through the expiry day`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `the temporary text ends on 31.8.2026 whatever happens to the Civic Service Law`

`moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text reading declined` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `a later Act moved the expiry to` (YMD 2027 8 31)
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the Law is in force through the expiry day`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `what ends the temporary text is declined`

`moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself out of force` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `a later Act moved the expiry to` (YMD 2027 8 31)
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the Law ends at the start of the expiry day`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `the temporary text ends with the Civic Service Law, whenever that is`

`the expiry as stated, the day itself declined, the temporary text fixed` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `the expiry stays as the deposited text states it`
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the expiry day itself is declined`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `the temporary text ends on 31.8.2026 whatever happens to the Civic Service Law`

`the moved-expiry reading declined, the day itself in force, the temporary text fixed` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `whether a later Act moved the expiry is declined`
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the Law is in force through the expiry day`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `the temporary text ends on 31.8.2026 whatever happens to the Civic Service Law`

`the moved-expiry reading declined, the day itself out of force` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `whether a later Act moved the expiry is declined`
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the Law ends at the start of the expiry day`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `the temporary text ends with the Civic Service Law, whenever that is`

§§ `s 36(a): is the Law in force on a day`

-- The printed day, and the published constants.
#ASSERT `National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) — the expiry day, as the deposited text states it` EQUALS YMD 2026 8 31
#ASSERT `National-Civic Service Law — the last day on which its commencement day may fall, from s 37(f)` EQUALS YMD 2014 6 30

-- At the deposited expiry, the day itself in force: 30.8.2026 yes, 31.8.2026 yes (the day itself), 1.9.2026 no.
#ASSERT     `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 30) `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
#ASSERT     `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
#ASSERT NOT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 9 1)  `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`

-- The day itself out of force: 30.8 yes, 31.8 no, 1.9 no.
#ASSERT     `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 30) `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself out of force`
#ASSERT NOT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself out of force`
#ASSERT NOT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 9 1)  `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself out of force`

-- Moved to 31.8.2027 (day itself in force): 1.9.2026 yes, 31.8.2027 yes, 1.9.2027 no.
#ASSERT     `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 9 1)  `, reading its expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text following`
#ASSERT     `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2027 8 31) `, reading its expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text following`
#ASSERT NOT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2027 9 1)  `, reading its expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text following`
-- ... and with the day itself out of force, 31.8.2027 no.
#ASSERT NOT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2027 8 31) `, reading its expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself out of force`

-- The Law's commencement is not in the text: a day on or before 30.6.2014 is declined, and the day after is not.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2014 6 30) `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force` BECAUSE "the commencement day of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited text, and it falls on or before 30 June 2014"
#ASSERT     `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2014 7 1) `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`

-- The expiry day itself, with its reading declined: refused by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, reading its expiry as` `the expiry as stated, the day itself declined, the temporary text fixed` BECAUSE "s 36(a) says the Law stands until a day and does not say whether that day itself is a day of the Law"
-- ... but not the day before it.
#ASSERT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 30) `, reading its expiry as` `the expiry as stated, the day itself declined, the temporary text fixed`

§§ `s 36(a) at the switch: a later Act may have moved the day`

-- At the switch (moved-expiry reading declined, day itself declined): up to 30.8.2026 every reading says yes.
#ASSERT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2025 12 31)
#ASSERT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 30)
-- 31.8.2026: the day-itself reading decides at the printed day, so the switch declines it by that name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 31) BECAUSE "s 36(a) says the Law stands until a day and does not say whether that day itself is a day of the Law"
-- 1.9.2026: no at the printed day, yes if it was moved: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 10 9) BECAUSE "whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts, and the answer turns on it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2027 3 1) BECAUSE "whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts, and the answer turns on it"

-- Only the moved-expiry reading declined, the day itself IN force: 31.8.2026 is yes under every reading (printed day, day in force; any later day, yes).
#ASSERT `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, reading its expiry as` `the moved-expiry reading declined, the day itself in force, the temporary text fixed`
-- ... and the day itself OUT of force: no at the printed day, yes if moved: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, reading its expiry as` `the moved-expiry reading declined, the day itself out of force` BECAUSE "whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts, and the answer turns on it"

§§ `s 36(b): the Law goes on applying to one who began before the expiry`

-- Served on 9.10.2026 (after the printed day), began 1.7.2026 (before it): the Law applies to him, whatever happens to the day.
#ASSERT `s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, serving on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9) `is` TRUE `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
#ASSERT `s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, serving on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9) `is` TRUE `, reading its expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text following`
#ASSERT `s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, serving on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9) `is` TRUE `, reading its expiry as` `the moved-expiry reading declined, the day itself out of force`
-- At the switch the same person is answered (the printed day answers TRUE).
#ASSERT `s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, serving on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9) `is` TRUE `, reading its expiry as` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36 — the readings this row takes where the texts do not decide`)

-- Began ON the printed day: not "before" it. On 9.10.2026 the Law is out of force at the printed day: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, serving on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9) `is` TRUE `, reading its expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
-- ... yes if the expiry was moved to 31.8.2027 (the Law is in force on 9.10.2026) ...
#ASSERT `s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, serving on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9) `is` TRUE `, reading its expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text following`
-- ... and declined at the switch, because the two differ.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, serving on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9) `is` TRUE `, reading its expiry as` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36 — the readings this row takes where the texts do not decide`) BECAUSE "whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts, and the answer turns on it"

-- A person not serving on the day is not reached, under every reading (no refusal: the readings agree).
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, serving on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9) `is` FALSE `, reading its expiry as` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36 — the readings this row takes where the texts do not decide`)

§ `Tests: National Insurance Law s 348(e), the temporary text`

§§ `Fixtures`

`September 2026` MEANS `A span of whole months of one tax year` WITH `the tax year` IS 2026, `the first month` IS 9, `the last month` IS 9
`August 2026`    MEANS `A span of whole months of one tax year` WITH `the tax year` IS 2026, `the first month` IS 8, `the last month` IS 8
`the third quarter of 2026` MEANS `A span of whole months of one tax year` WITH `the tax year` IS 2026, `the first month` IS 7, `the last month` IS 9
`the fourth quarter of 2026` MEANS `A span of whole months of one tax year` WITH `the tax year` IS 2026, `the first month` IS 10, `the last month` IS 12
`the whole of 2026` MEANS `A span of whole months of one tax year` WITH `the tax year` IS 2026, `the first month` IS 1, `the last month` IS 12
`December 2026` MEANS `A span of whole months of one tax year` WITH `the tax year` IS 2026, `the first month` IS 12, `the last month` IS 12

§§ `The span's days`

-- September 2026 runs 1.9 to 30.9; the fourth quarter ends 31.12 (the last month is 12, so the year is carried).
#ASSERT `the first day of the span` `September 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 9 1
#ASSERT `the last day of the span, as a day count` `September 2026` EQUALS Day (YMD 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT `the last day of the span, as a day count` `the fourth quarter of 2026` EQUALS Day (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `the last day of the span, as a day count` `August 2026` EQUALS Day (YMD 2026 8 31)

§§ `At the printed day (the expiry as stated, the temporary text following)`

-- The cases of row IL-05's tests (its lines 458-466), put as the yes or no they turn on.
-- Began 1.9.2025, September 2026: began before 31.8.2026: yes.
#ASSERT     `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, for the span` `September 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
-- Began 30.8.2026, September 2026: before 31.8.2026: yes.
#ASSERT     `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 8 30) `, for the span` `September 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
-- Began 31.8.2026, September 2026: not before it; the span begins after it: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, for the span` `September 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
-- Began 31.8.2026, August 2026: the span ends on 31.8.2026, by the expiry: yes.
#ASSERT     `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, for the span` `August 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
-- Began 31.8.2026, the third quarter: the span (1.7 to 30.9) straddles 31.8 and he did not begin before it: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, for the span` `the third quarter of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force` BECAUSE "the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this span, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends"
-- Began 15.9.2026, the fourth quarter: the span begins after 31.8.2026: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 9 15) `, for the span` `the fourth quarter of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
-- Began 15.9.2026, the third quarter: it straddles and he began after: declined (not "no"): the part of the quarter before the expiry is not apportioned.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 9 15) `, for the span` `the third quarter of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force` BECAUSE "the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this span, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends"
-- Began 1.9.2025, the whole of 2026: before the expiry: yes.
#ASSERT     `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, for the span` `the whole of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`
-- Began 1.1.2026, the whole of 2026: before 31.8.2026: yes.
#ASSERT     `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, for the span` `the whole of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the deposited expiry, the day itself in force`

§§ `Moved to 31.8.2027`

-- The temporary text follows the Law: it ends 31.8.2027. Began 15.9.2026, the fourth quarter of 2026 ends 31.12.2026, by 31.8.2027: yes.
#ASSERT     `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 9 15) `, for the span` `the fourth quarter of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text following`
-- The temporary text fixed at 31.8.2026: began 15.9.2026, the fourth quarter: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 9 15) `, for the span` `the fourth quarter of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text fixed`
-- Its reading declined: the two ends give yes and no: declined by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 9 15) `, for the span` `the fourth quarter of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text reading declined` BECAUSE "whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts, and the answer turns on it"
-- ... but a person who began before 31.8.2026 gets yes at both ends.
#ASSERT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, for the span` `the fourth quarter of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `moved to 31.8.2027, the day itself in force, the temporary text reading declined`
-- Moved, and the span straddles the NEW end: began 31.8.2027, a span of the third quarter of 2027 is not built here; the straddle at the printed day is tested above.

§§ `At the switch (every reading declined)`

-- Answered where the printed day answers yes (it never falls as the day moves later): the cases of the first section.
#ASSERT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, for the span` `September 2026`
#ASSERT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 8 30) `, for the span` `September 2026`
#ASSERT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, for the span` `August 2026`
#ASSERT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, for the span` `the whole of 2026`
-- Declined where the printed day says no, because a moved expiry would say yes.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, for the span` `September 2026` BECAUSE "whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts, and the answer turns on it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 9 15) `, for the span` `the fourth quarter of 2026` BECAUSE "whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts, and the answer turns on it"
-- At the straddle the printed day itself declines, by its own name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, for the span` `the third quarter of 2026` BECAUSE "the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this span, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends"
-- With the temporary text FIXED at 31.8.2026 the moved-expiry reading no longer matters: answered, whatever it is.
#ASSERT NOT `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` (YMD 2026 9 15) `, for the span` `the fourth quarter of 2026` `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` `the moved-expiry reading declined, the day itself in force, the temporary text fixed`
